  "question": {
    "text": "The value of the acceleration due to gravity is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> at a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo></math> radius of the earth) from the surface of the earth. It is again equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> at a depth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> below the surface the earth. The ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math> equals:"
